        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend-stack-15-text" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;one per backing service&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="382" y="2094" width="208" height="22" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-legend-notes" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;Large dashed frame: infra perimeter · small: functional group&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;⚠ Gx&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;: docs and code disagree, see &quot;Gaps&quot;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="2370" width="520" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-steps" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#059669&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Request path · Apply (S4)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; An admin or owner applies the draft; the CMP asks for a passkey step-up first.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; The import module writes the import rows and dispatches the build workflow with ids and the SHA only.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;3&lt;/span&gt; Job prepare mints a CNP-Import token for the one repo, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;4&lt;/span&gt; downloads the tarball at that SHA, runs gitleaks and trivy fs. No user code runs with a secret.&lt;br&gt;• Job build has no secret and no id-token: buildx, Trivy image, Syft SBOM.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;5&lt;/span&gt; Job publish pushes ghcr.io/3-istor/imports/&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;app&amp;gt; by digest, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;6&lt;/span&gt; then calls the CMP back with its GitHub OIDC JWT.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;7&lt;/span&gt; One Git Data commit writes values, digests and dependsOn to the registry, as CNP-Portal. An app enters spec.apps with its first digest.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;8&lt;/span&gt; The ApplicationSet picks the record up and creates the Applications, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;9&lt;/span&gt; which render infra-templates with $values from cnp-projects, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;10&lt;/span&gt; and apply the workloads.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;11&lt;/span&gt; The kubelet pulls the image by digest with the project pull credential. &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;12&lt;/span&gt; The CMP reads Application health, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;13&lt;/span&gt; then runs a smoke check (the project policy lets arcl-cmp in).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="640" y="1860" width="780" height="560" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-bg" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#7c3aed&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Background · linking, analysis, rebuild&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;A&lt;/span&gt; The user installs CNP-Import on chosen repos; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;C&lt;/span&gt; the CMP proves it with the OAuth user token and GET /user/installations (S1).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt; GitLab: OAuth with PKCE, &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;D&lt;/span&gt; tokens kept encrypted (S2).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;E&lt;/span&gt; Analysis (S3): &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;F&lt;/span&gt; the analyzer downloads a size-capped tarball at the SHA, &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;G&lt;/span&gt; or the GitLab archive; it parses compose, Dockerfiles, poms and nginx, and executes nothing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;H&lt;/span&gt; GitHub push webhook (HMAC), &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;I&lt;/span&gt; GitLab polling every 5 min: both start a rebuild (S5).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;J&lt;/span&gt; A Terraform run in the CMP pod writes the backing apps&amp;#39; generated credentials to Vault kvv2 project-&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;app&amp;gt;, after the build passed. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;M&lt;/span&gt; The CMP already reads VictoriaMetrics; the Topology tab adds observed flows (view topology-data).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;K&lt;/span&gt; GitLab builds: job prepare trades its OIDC JWT for a short GitLab token, &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;L&lt;/span&gt; then downloads the archive. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;N&lt;/span&gt; The wizard and the draft canvas. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;O&lt;/span&gt; An imported service reaches its backing app through a dependsOn alias.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1460" y="1860" width="760" height="380" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-trust" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#e11d48&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Who touches the user&amp;#39;s code&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Read only, short lived.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; CNP-Import (contents:read, metadata:read) and GitLab OAuth (read_repository, read_api); tokens of 1 hour, scoped to one repo for a build.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Argo CD never reads a user repo.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; It reads cnp-projects and infra-templates; images come by digest from GHCR.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;The user repo stays the source of truth.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; CNP writes nothing to it: no deploy/values, no Image Updater.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2260" y="1860" width="680" height="380" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-gaps" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ea580c&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Gaps between docs and code&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;GI1&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;CNP-Portal on user accounts.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; The CMP already sends users to install CNP-Portal on their own account (user_github_installations). The design forbids it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;GI2&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Step-up is off.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; STEP_UP_ENABLED defaults to false: Apply would run on a plain session.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;GI4&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;AppProject trusts every repoURL.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; sourceRepos lists each spec.apps[].repoURL: an imported app must carry source, not repoURL.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Registry writes.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Today one Contents API PUT per change; the design moves to one Git Data API commit per apply or callback.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1460" y="2260" width="1480" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
